According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global AI-powered robot vacuum cleaner market was valued at USD 798 million in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 1,296 million by 2031, growing at a CAGR of 7.5% during the forecast period (2025–2031). This robust growth is driven by increasing adoption of smart home technologies, advancements in AI-powered navigation systems, and rising demand for time-saving home appliances.
What are AI-Powered Robot Vacuum Cleaners?
AI-powered robot vacuum cleaners are autonomous floor-cleaning devices that utilize artificial intelligence algorithms, LiDAR navigation, and computer vision to efficiently clean homes with minimal human intervention. These intelligent systems can map living spaces, avoid obstacles, and adapt cleaning patterns based on different surface types. Advanced models now incorporate features like self-emptying dustbins, mopping capabilities, and integration with smart home ecosystems through IoT connectivity.
Leading brands such as iRobot (Roomba), Ecovacs, and Roborock have set industry standards with their AI-driven cleaning solutions that offer scheduled cleaning, voice control compatibility, and real-time monitoring through smartphone apps. The technology has evolved significantly from early random-path models to sophisticated systems that can create detailed 3D maps of homes with 90% accuracy.
